## Benefit Analysis: Avoided-Purchase and Storage Savings
The Phase 1 Expected Benefits section states the financial benefit qualitatively: “reduced
spending by reusing surplus assets and lowering storage costs.” This section quantifies that
benefit directly, using the avoided purchase price of reused assets together with clearly stated
assumptions so every figure can be checked and adjusted. The formula and assumptions
below do exactly that, cross-checked where possible against a simulated stakeholder
interview (Appendix A).
Avoided-Purchase Savings = Number of Assets Reused × Average Avoided Purchase
Price (6)
Assumption (reuse volume): using the same 150-active-user pilot base introduced above
under Recurring (Operational) Costs, the team assumes roughly 1 completed reuse
transaction for every 4 active users over the semester (150 ÷ 4 ≈ 37, rounded to 40 assets).
This is a conservative, illustrative figure for an early-stage internal exchange pilot, not a KU-
specific historical statistic, since itemized KU reuse or purchase records are not publicly
available. A simulated University Management (Customer) Representative (AI Stakeholder
Mimic; see Appendix A, Q1) described a realistic first-semester pilot as “a handful of
departments… in the range of a hundred to a couple hundred active participants,” which is
consistent with the 150-user scale used here.
Assumption (avoided unit price): AED 551 average avoided purchase price per reused
asset, a blended estimate across the low-to-mid-value campus items the Phase 1 report
describes ReSource handling (furniture, lab equipment accessories, electronics peripherals,
and office supplies). The same simulated University Management Representative (Appendix
A, Q2) described the assets most likely to go through the system as “the everyday stuff
departments accumulate… individually low-to-mid value items, not major capital equipment,”
which supports keeping this estimate in the low-to-mid range rather than assuming higher-
value equipment.
Avoided-Purchase Savings = 40 assets × AED 551 = AED 22,040 (per pilot semester)
(7)
Assumption (storage/handling savings): AED 18 per asset in avoided storage and handling
